# False positive: `private_key=key_bytes` is a keyword argument to
# grpc.ssl_channel_credentials() where `key_bytes` is a variable holding the
# client's TLS private key material already supplied via the relation
# databag, not a hardcoded secret. The generic-api-key rule matches on the
# `private_key=` keyword alone. This finding is on a commit from an open,
# unmerged branch (SQT-928-etcd-persistence) that gitleaks' default `--all`
# git-log scan picks up regardless of which branch/PR triggered the scan.
